entry.summary:
TRAITS in PHP
Solve code reuse problems in single inheritance languages like PHP.


Avoid duplicating methods across unrelated classes.


Helps organize reusable behavior (like logging, auth, etc.)



trait Logger {
    public function log(string $message) {
        echo "[LOG] $message\n";
    }
}

class Order {
    use Logger;

    public function process() {
        $this->log("Order processed.");
    }
}

$order = new Order();
$order->process(); // Output: [LOG] Order processed.


Traits and Name Collisions
trait A {
    public function test() { echo "A"; }
}

trait B {
    public function test() { echo "B"; }
}

class MyClass {
    use A, B {
        B::test insteadof A;
        A::test as testA;
    }
}


*using traits from one file to another file *
✅ 1. Define the Trait in One File…
